<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Holy Alliance</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1815</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Holy Alliance was an agreement signed in September 1815 by the rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, proposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a>, by which they pledged to govern according to Christian principles. Under Metternich's influence it came to stand for the conservative powers' cooperation in suppressing liberal and national revolutions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holy-alliance.jpg" alt="Holy Alliance" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cukrakalnis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Holy_Alliance_(1840).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
